{
  "finding": "On tmpfs the fastest store at 8 workers is still a plain per-worker mmap. MAP_POPULATE, MADV_POPULATE_WRITE, MADV_HUGEPAGE, O_DIRECT and sync_file_range are slower there, and shmem_enabled is never so a huge-page advice does not change the backing. On ext4 one fallocate of the whole file then the mapped write is the fastest synthetic store, by about 13 ms at 8 threads and 2 ms at 8 processes. Putting that reservation into the writer moved the real ext4 thread writes by about 10 ms, inside camp12's interquartile range, and switching ext4 ranks from pwrite onto the mapping made them slower. The writer keeps the current store.",
